    276          /**
    277           *  @brief      Startup observer for PMSM motor.
    278           *  @details
    279           *
    280           * That observer estimates two electrical speeds according to the following equations:
    281           *
    282           *
    283           * \f[
    284           *  \begin{aligned}
    285           *     &\hat{\omega_d} = V_d \cdot \left[-\frac{1}{L_s I_q}\right]\\
    286           *     &\hat{\omega_d} = (V_q - V_{qAlign}) \cdot \frac{1}{\varphi_m}\\
    287           *  \end{aligned}
    288           * \f]
    289           *
    290           * where
    291           *
    292           * \f$ V_{d} \f$: voltage on d axis
    293           *
    294           * \f$ V_{q} \f$: voltage on q axis
    295           *
    296           * \f$ I_{q} \f$: current on q axis
    297           *
    298           * \f$ \hat{omega_{d}} \f$: estimated speed based on d axis equation
    299           *
    300           * \f$ \hat{omega_{q}} \f$: estimated speed based on q axis equation
    301           *
    302           * \f$ -\left[\frac{1}{L_s I_q}\right] = K1 \f$
    303           *
    304           * \f$ \frac{1}{\varphi_m} = K2 \f$
    305           *
    306           * The error is given by:
    307           *
    308           * \f$ \omega_{error} = \hat{\omega_{d}} - \hat{\omega_{q}} \f$
